            {
              "id": "79a40598-8a64-3f91-b5e2-e0d14a99e0e0",
              "name": "\"XSS Vulnerabilities from User-Controlled Data in innerHTML, outerHTML, and document.write Methods\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in question is a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability that arises from user-controlled data in `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, and `document.write` methods in JavaScript. XSS vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript.\n\nIn the provided code, the `innerHTML` property is used to add HTML content to a `span` element. If the `c.property` value is controlled by the user and is not properly sanitized, it can lead to an XSS vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, and `document.write` methods with user-controlled data. Instead, use safer alternatives like `textContent` or `innerText` which do not interpret the passed content as HTML.\n\nIf you must use these methods, ensure that user-controlled data is properly sanitized before use. This can be done using a trusted library or framework that automatically escapes user-controlled data, or by manually escaping special characters.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the line:\n\n```javascript\nb.innerHTML=c.property;\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```javascript\nb.textContent=c.property;\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to depend on the following libraries:\n\n- dat.GUI\n- A library represented by the variable `g`, which provides a `addClass` function. This could be a library like jQuery.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
