            {
              "id": "fa296d68-ad40-3734-bc51-170d1da75421",
              "name": "\"XSS Vulnerabilities from User-Controlled Data in innerHTML, outerHTML, and document.write Methods\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. In this case, the vulnerability arises from user-controlled data in `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, and `document.write` methods in JavaScript.\n\nThe specific sink in the provided code is the `innerHTML` method, which is used to manipulate the content of an HTML element. If the data passed to this method is user-controlled and not properly sanitized, it can lead to an XSS vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, and `document.write` to inject user-controlled data into the DOM. Instead, use safer alternatives like `textContent` or `innerText` that do not interpret the passed data as HTML.\n\nIf you must use these methods, ensure that the data is properly sanitized before it is passed to them. This can be done using a library that provides HTML sanitization, or by implementing a strict Content Security Policy (CSP) that disallows inline scripts.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the vulnerable line:\n\n```javascript\na.__preset_select[b].innerHTML=a.__preset_select[b].value;\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```javascript\na.__preset_select[b].textContent=a.__preset_select[b].value;\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example does not provide enough context to determine the required library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
