              "id": "ad99225a-d110-3e75-ada8-ce211f047809",
              "name": "\"XSS Vulnerabilities from User-Controlled Data in Methods like `innerHTML`, `outerHTML`, or `document.write`\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn the provided code, the vulnerability lies in the use of `innerHTML` method. This method can lead to XSS attacks if the data being passed to it is controlled by the user and not properly sanitized.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate XSS vulnerabilities, you should:\n\n- Use the principle of least privilege. Only necessary permissions should be granted, and they should be granted for the shortest time possible.\n- Validate and sanitize all user inputs. All user-controlled data should be considered untrusted.\n- Use secure APIs that automatically escape XSS, such as `innerText` instead of `innerHTML`.\n- Use Content Security Policy (CSP) to reduce the severity of any XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `innerHTML` method with `innerText` or `textContent`:\n\n```javascript\nthis.__closeButton=document.createElement(\"div\");\nthis.__closeButton.textContent=m.TEXT_CLOSED;\ng.addClass(this.__closeButton,m.CLASS_CLOSE_BUTTON);\nthis.domElement.appendChild(this.__closeButton);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code seems to be using a custom library `g` for DOM manipulation and event handling. The exact dependencies cannot be determined without more context.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
