              "id": "0ad097b9-6467-365b-853b-54e39946588a",
              "name": "\"Vulnerability Detected in Unmaintained `notevil` Package; `eval` Package Suggested as Safer Alternative\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `notevil` package in JavaScript is a safer version of `eval()`, which is a function that executes JavaScript code represented as a string. However, a vulnerability has been detected in the `notevil` package, which is no longer maintained. This vulnerability could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code, leading to serious security issues such as data breaches or server takeovers.\n\nThe `eval` package is suggested as a safer alternative to `notevil`. It provides a similar functionality but is actively maintained and has additional security measures to prevent code injection attacks.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to replace the `notevil` package with the `eval` package. Avoid using `eval()` or similar functions that execute code represented as a string, as they are often a source of code injection vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `notevil` package with the `eval` package in your code. Here is an example of how to do it:\n\n```javascript\nconst safeEval = require('safe-eval');\nconst context = { orderLinesData: 'your data here' };\nconst code = 'your code here';\nconst result = safeEval(code, context);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the `safe-eval` package to execute properly.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 2017: A1-Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A1_2017-Injection)\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet: Injection Prevention](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)\n\nPlease note that all links were active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing this report."
              },
