            {
              "id": "366e4961-7722-3bdd-9e93-ed0a79e7b0bd",
              "name": "Potential Code Injection Vulnerability Detected through eval() Usage",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `eval()` function in JavaScript is a powerful feature that allows the execution of arbitrary JavaScript code. However, it is also a common source of code injection vulnerabilities. If an attacker can control the input to `eval()`, they can execute arbitrary JavaScript code in the context of your application. This can lead to a variety of attacks, including data theft, denial of service, and remote code execution.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, `eval(expression)` is used to evaluate a JavaScript expression. If the `expression` variable can be controlled by an attacker, this could lead to a code injection vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nAvoid using `eval()` whenever possible. In many cases, there are safer alternatives to `eval()`. For example, if you need to parse JSON data, use `JSON.parse()` instead.\n\nIf you absolutely must use `eval()`, make sure to properly sanitize and validate the input. Never trust user input. Consider using a safe, context-specific encoding library to encode user input before passing it to `eval()`.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```javascript\n// Instead of using eval(), consider using safer alternatives.\n// For example, if `expression` is a JSON string, you can use JSON.parse().\n\ntry {\n    const answer = JSON.parse(expression).toString();\n} catch (error) {\n    console.error(\"Invalid JSON expression: \", error);\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet does not require any library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 2017: Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A1_2017-Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-94"
                ]
              }
