              "id": "6c21e221-4e0a-3903-a59d-e06db991296b",
              "name": "Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability\" in JavaScript is a security flaw that allows unauthorized users to view a list of all files in a directory due to the server being configured to provide a file index. This can lead to information disclosure as sensitive files or data might be exposed to attackers.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the `serveIndex` middleware is used to serve directory listings. The directory 'logs' is exposed with detailed view and icons, which could potentially disclose sensitive information in the log files.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should disable directory listing for your application. If directory listing is necessary for some reason, ensure that it is only enabled for directories that do not contain sensitive information.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nYou can disable directory listing by not using the `serveIndex` middleware for sensitive directories. If you need to serve static files from a directory, use the `express.static` middleware instead. Here is how you can modify the provided code snippet:\n\n```javascript\nvar express = require('express');\nvar app = express();\n\napp.use('/support/logs', express.static('logs'));\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- express\n- serve-index\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Insecure Direct Object References](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A5_2017-Broken_Access_Control)\n- [CWE-548: Information Exposure Through Directory Listing](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/548.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-548",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/548.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-548"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "f22e7ad8-dd96-3a2c-95ef-c3940facde39",
              "name": "Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability\" in JavaScript, particularly in Node.js applications, is a security flaw that allows unauthorized users to list all files in a directory that is served by the application. This can lead to information disclosure as sensitive files or data might be exposed to attackers.\n\nIn the provided code, the `serveIndex` middleware is used to serve the directory listing of the `encryptionkeys` directory. This can be a serious security issue if the directory contains sensitive data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should disable directory listing for all sensitive directories. If directory listing is required for some reason, make sure to protect it with proper authentication and authorization checks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nYou can disable directory listing by not using the `serveIndex` middleware for sensitive directories. Here is how you can fix the provided code:\n\n```javascript\napp.use('/encryptionkeys', express.static('encryptionkeys'));\n```\n\nIn this fixed code, the `express.static` middleware is used instead of `serveIndex`. This middleware serves the files in the directory as static resources, but it does not allow directory listing.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- express\n- serve-index\n\nYou can install them using npm:\n\n```bash\nnpm install express serve-index\n```\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Node.js Security Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-548: Information Exposure Through Directory Listing](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/548.html)"
              },
