              "name": "Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Enabled Directory Listing/Indexing Vulnerability\" in JavaScript is a security flaw that allows unauthorized users to list all files in a directory due to the server being improperly configured. This can lead to information disclosure as attackers can discover files not intended for their view. In the provided code snippet, the vulnerability lies in the `serveIndex` middleware which is used to serve an index of the 'ftp' directory.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should disable directory listing in your application. If directory listing is necessary, ensure that it is properly protected with authentication and authorization controls. Also, sensitive files should not be stored in directories that allow listing.\n\n## Source Code Fix\n\nTo fix the vulnerability in the provided code snippet, you can remove the `serveIndex` middleware:\n\n```javascript\napp.use('/ftp', serveIndexMiddleware)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Express.js\n- serve-index\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-548: Information Exposure Through Directory Listing](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/548.html)"
