            {
              "id": "a1497581-ae92-38f7-b69c-4c110641874d",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nA potential Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability can occur when user-controlled data is used in an HTML string. This can allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users. In the provided JavaScript code, the error message is being logged with user-controlled data, which could potentially be exploited if the logged data is later displayed in an HTML context.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to properly escape user-controlled data before using it in an HTML context. This can be done using various methods, such as HTML encoding, JavaScript encoding, or URL encoding, depending on the context.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, the `utils.getErrorMessage(err)` function is potentially returning user-controlled data. This data should be properly escaped before being used. Here is a fixed version of the code:\n\n```javascript\nconst errorMessage = utils.getErrorMessage(err);\nconst safeErrorMessage = escape(errorMessage);\nlogger.error(`Could not insert Complaint: ${safeErrorMessage}`);\n```\n\nIn this fixed version, the `escape` function is used to escape any potentially harmful characters in the error message. Note that the `escape` function is a built-in JavaScript function and does not require any additional library dependencies.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code does not specify any library dependencies. However, it is assumed that `logger` and `utils` are either built-in objects or are imported from external libraries.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/)\n- [XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
